    "description": "MOSDAC - Meteorological and Oceanographic Satellite Data Archival Center\n•Implemented a module to predict real time cyclone activities using different algorithms and various form of data.\n•Designed and implemented REST APIs for weather forecast events using JSON, Java, Oracle as a database, satellite product visualization and converter tools.\n•Developed different modules like user management, data source management, data selection and visualization, portal management, report generation, grid and location wise forecast and user questionnaires using technologies such as Java, Spring MVC, Hibernate, JSP/Servlet and Oracle 10g as a database.\n•Developed and enhanced the data request module that provides national satellite metadata and also download the data to register users on FTP site.\n•Responsible for developing backend efficient software for real time data update on the MOSDAC and other desktop applications. \n•Implemented a feature to pull large-scale data from different locations, push it to user space, archive the data and finally serve on the MOSDAC portal using core Java, multithreading, collection, Oracle 10g database and Linux.\n•Enhanced the exception handling and improved the quality by introducing Junit testing.\n•Performed parameterization of the automated test scripts in selenium to check how the application\nperforms against multiple sets of data.\nCALVAL - Calibration and Validation website\n•Designed and developed CALVAL web site that facilitates the archival, visualization and dissemination of the data for scientific interpretation and analysis for various mission using Struts MVC, JSP/Servlet.\n•Involved in JUnit test cases for testing the model classes, Identified test data based upon the test cases and created test suites using JAVA, XML, TestNG.\n•Developed business logic for generates images using HDF5, creates thumbnails of daily satellites images and shows total received images for the date wise analysis of image dissemination & monitoring.\n\n\n",
